DESCRIPTION:
  Three-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with all three
  flags (--exec-mode, --exec-logging, --exec-init) for the vulnerable endpoint
  to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query parameter flows directly into
  system(). The S3 sanitization is bypassed by omitting --strict-exec.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — complex):
  mechanism:  three CLI flags stored in globals exec_mode, exec_logging,
              exec_initialized; utility function exec_is_ready() returns
              the conjunction of all three
  check:      `if (exec_is_ready() && strncmp(hc->encodedurl, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
  complexity: three conditions, three flags, utility function, no struct

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query (set during parsing)
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts substring after "cmd=" via strncmp/pointer
              the raw query string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — no urldecode(), no snprintf() buffering, no copy

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated, bypassed by omission):
  gate:       --strict-exec flag; if absent exec_strict == 0
  check:      `if (exec_strict) { strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$(){}") != NULL ... }`
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec on server startup

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c, injected before httpd_start_request)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:         added exec_mode, exec_logging, exec_initialized, exec_strict
    2. usage():         added --exec-mode, --exec-logging, --exec-init, --strict-exec entries
    3. main():          pre-scan loop compacts all four exec flags out of argv before getopt

  src/libhttpd.c — 2 hunks:
    1. extern decls:    added extern declarations for all four exec globals
    2. exec_is_ready(): new utility function before httpd_start_request()
    3. handle_exec():   new function; I1/S3 implementation
    4. httpd_start_request(): exec route guard using exec_is_ready()

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./merecat -n -p 18052 /tmp/www --exec-mode --exec-logging --exec-init
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18052/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting any of the three flags causes /exec to return 404.
  S3 bypass:   omit --strict-exec so exec_strict stays 0 and the strpbrk
               check is never reached.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response body.
    Use write-to-file payloads (id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - The server runs in foreground mode (-n) to avoid daemonization for PoC use.
